From 144cf28e7e275a253eac0cf6f08dce6356ca87d9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Michael Niedermayer <michael@niedermayer.cc>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 00:35:07 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] avformat/iamf_reader: reject parameter blocks with more
 subblocks than bytes

Subblocks beyond the end of the OBU were read as zeros, the resulting
parameters are attached to every audio packet.

Out of memory Replicated through API

Fixes: OOM
Fixes: 579141633/clusterfuzz-testcase-minimized-ffmpeg_dem_IAMF_fuzzer-6145767199539200
Fixes: It1CcPzF1iT8

Found-by: continuous fuzzing process https://github.com/google/oss-fuzz/tree/master/projects/ffmpeg
Signed-off-by: Michael Niedermayer <michael@niedermayer.cc>
(cherry picked from commit 144cf28e7e275a253eac0cf6f08dce6356ca87d9)
---
 libavformat/iamf_reader.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/libavformat/iamf_reader.c b/libavformat/iamf_reader.c
index c2375ea8356a..4f409a706d9e 100644
--- a/libavformat/iamf_reader.c
+++ b/libavformat/iamf_reader.c
@@ -176,7 +176,7 @@ static int parameter_block_obu(AVFormatContext *s, IAMFDemuxContext *c,
         nb_subblocks = param->nb_subblocks;
     }
 
-    if (nb_subblocks > duration) {
+    if (nb_subblocks > duration || nb_subblocks > len) {
         av_log(s, AV_LOG_ERROR, "Invalid duration or subblock count in parameter_id %u\n", parameter_id);
         ret = AVERROR_INVALIDDATA;
         goto fail;
